<div id=3D"footer-outer" data-cols=3D"4" data-custom-color=3D"false" data-d=
isable-copyright=3D"false" data-matching-section-color=3D"true" data-copyri=
ght-line=3D"false" data-using-bg-img=3D"false" data-bg-img-overlay=3D"1.0" =
data-full-width=3D"1" data-using-widget-area=3D"true" data-link-hover=3D"de=
fault">
<div id=3D"footer-widgets" data-has-widgets=3D"true" data-cols=3D"4">
<div class=3D"container">
<div class=3D"row">
<div class=3D"col span_3 one-fourths clear-both">
<div id=3D"text-17" class=3D"widget widget_text"><h4>About the Cancer Imagi=
ng Archive (TCIA)</h4>			<div class=3D"textwidget"><p><strong>TCIA is a ser=
vice which de-identifies and hosts a large archive of medical images of can=
cer</strong> accessible for public download. The data are organized as =E2=
=80=9Ccollections=E2=80=9D; typically patients=E2=80=99 imaging related by =
a common disease (e.g. lung cancer), image modality or type (MRI, CT, digit=
al histopathology, etc) or research focus. DICOM is the primary file format=
 used by TCIA for radiology imaging. Supporting data related to the images =
such as patient outcomes, treatment details, genomics and expert analyses a=
re also provided when available.</p>
<p><a href=3D"https://www.cancerimagingarchive.net/about-the-cancer-imaging=
-archive-tcia/">Read more=E2=80=A6</a></p>
</div>
</div>					</div>
<div class=3D"col span_3 one-fourths right-edge">
<div id=3D"text-19" class=3D"widget widget_text"><h4>About the Cancer Imagi=
ng Program (CIP)</h4>			<div class=3D"textwidget"><p>The Cancer Imaging Pro=
gram (CIP) is one of four Programs in the Division of&nbsp;<a href=3D"https=
://dctd.cancer.gov/">Cancer Treatment and Diagnosis (DCTD)</a>&nbsp;of the&=
nbsp;<a href=3D"https://www.cancer.gov/">National Cancer Institute</a>. For=
 complete information about the Cancer Imaging Program, please see the&nbsp=
;<a href=3D"https://imaging.cancer.gov/">Cancer Imaging Program Website</a>=
.</p>
<p><a href=3D"https://www.cancerimagingarchive.net/tcia-2019/about-the-canc=
er-imaging-program-cip/">Read more=E2=80=A6</a></p>
</div>
</div>							=09
</div>
<div class=3D"col span_3 one-fourths clear-both">
<div id=3D"text-18" class=3D"widget widget_text"><h4>Hosting TCIA at UAMS</=
h4>			<div class=3D"textwidget"><p>In October 2015 Dr. Prior and the core T=
CIA team relocated from Washington University to the&nbsp;<a href=3D"https:=
//dbmi.uams.edu/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener">Department of Biomedic=
al Informatics</a>&nbsp;at the&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://medicine.uams.edu/" =
target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener">University of Arkansas for Medical Scien=
ces</a>.&nbsp; The archive continues provides high quality, high value imag=
e collections to cancer researchers around the world.</p>
<p><a href=3D"https://www.cancerimagingarchive.net/about-the-university-of-=
arkansas-for-medical-sciences-uams/">Read more=E2=80=A6</a></p>
</div>
</div>								=09
</div>
<div class=3D"col span_3 one-fourths right-edge">
<div id=3D"text-20" class=3D"widget widget_text"><h4>About FNLCR</h4>			<di=
v class=3D"textwidget"><p>The Frederick National Laboratory for Cancer Rese=
arch (FNLCR) is a Federally Funded Research and Development Center dedicate=
d to the application of biomedical science and technology to improve human =
health. FNLCR scientists conduct basic, translational and applied research,=
 create new technologies, and collaborate with government, industry and aca=
demic colleagues to support the National Cancer Institute and other Institu=
tes of the National Institutes of Health.</p>
<p><a href=3D"https://www.cancerimagingarchive.net/about-frederick-national=
-laboratory-for-cancer-research/">Read more=E2=80=A6</a></p>
</div>
</div><div id=3D"custom_html-2" class=3D"widget_text widget widget_custom_h=
tml"><div class=3D"textwidget custom-html-widget"><!--
<a class=3D"twitter-timeline" data-lang=3D"en" data-height=3D"600" data-the=
me=3D"dark" href=3D"https://twitter.com/TCIA_News?ref_src=3Dtwsrc%5Etfw">Tw=
eets by TCIA_News</a> <script async src=3D"https://platform.twitter.com/wid=
gets.js" charset=3D"utf-8"></script>
-->
</div></div>									=09
</div>
</div>
</div><!--/container-->
</div><!--/footer-widgets-->
